## 7. File Modification Protocol

### Planning Mode File Modification Tool Sequence
```typescript
// 1. Read file before modification
read_file("[target_file]", should_read_entire_file=true)

// 2. Make changes directly
edit_file("[target_file]", 
          "Clear description of changes",
          "Actual content changes with precise formatting")

// 3. Verify changes were applied
read_file("[target_file]", [start_line], [line_count])
```

- **Direct File Editing**: ALWAYS use edit_file tools to make changes directly to files in Planning Mode
- **No Code Snippets in Responses**: NEVER respond with code blocks or snippet suggestions when actual file changes are requested
- **Verification Requirement**: After making file changes, verify the changes were successfully applied
- **Markdown Formatting**: Maintain consistent formatting in documentation files

