## 10. Autonomous Workflow Efficiency

### Mode Transition Best Practices
- Maintain complete separation of concerns between modes
- NO documentation updates in dev-mode
- NO code implementation in plan-mode
- Only ONE transition per implementation cycle (dev-mode to plan-mode)
- Stay in dev-mode until ALL implementation is complete and verified
- Switch to plan-mode ONLY after implementation is complete
- Signal transition clearly with "Implementation complete. Switching to Planning Mode..."
- Send implementation-and-documentation-complete ONLY in plan-mode

### Minimal Interaction Design
- Minimize required interactions from Tyler
- Make autonomous decisions on implementation approach
- Switch modes only at the single transition point
- Update ALL documentation after implementation is complete
- Focus on delivering complete, working implementations

